description:
Retrieve draft-mahy-mimi-identity and the other MIMI/MLS-related draft-mahy-* individual drafts, read each, and turn what they mean for mimid into beads. Requested by Mark 2026-10-19, prompted by rohanmahy pointing mimi-protocol#159's credential/domain question at draft-mahy-mimi-identity ('no WG consensus').

SCOPE RULE (constraint, not judgment): in scope = draft-mahy-mimi-*, draft-mahy-mls-*, draft-mahy-oob-aad, draft-mahy-cbor-edn-for-tls, draft-mahy-cbor-pointer, draft-mahy-lamps-im-keyusage, draft-mahy-vcon-mimi-messages, draft-mahy-dispatch-immi-*. Everything else draft-mahy-* (SIP, geopriv, xcap, enum, ...) is out. A draft that was replaced by a WG draft mimid already targets (AGENTS.md table: content, room-policy, ratchet-tree-options, pq-ciphersuites, ...) gets one line in the inventory and no assay. Datatracker listed 78 draft-mahy-* on 2026-10-19 (~35 in scope).

ASSAY OUTPUT CONTRACT (every assay bead): read the whole draft from ~/PROJECT/IETF/specs (never over the network), then file beads under this epic (or the owning epic) and list them in the assay bead's notes:
 - exactly one decision bead for Mark (label human): adopt now / adopt later / track only / ignore, with reasons; mimid targets WG drafts (lang-and-spec-target), so adopting an individual draft is Mark's call;
 - for each conflict with an existing mimid decision or code: a bead citing the draft section+line and the decision/file:line;
 - for each feature mimid would build if adopted: a task bead (filed only if Mark adopts; until then listed in the decision bead);
 - for each spec defect found: a wg bead (label wg, spec:<draft>-<rev>, per memory wg-feedback);
 - 'no impact' is a valid finding; say so in the notes.
Verify every claim against the text with line numbers (memory verify-before-asking). Assays are reading work: no code changes. Nothing is posted externally.
